<title>ITALY: Italy's Visco says VAT changes outlined.</title>
<headline>Italy's Visco says VAT changes outlined.</headline>
<text>
<p>ROME, May 30 (Italy) - Italy's Finance Minister Vincenzo Visco said on Monday the newly adopted three-year economic strategy outlines &quot;changes in principle&quot; to certain value added tax rates.</p>
<p>Visco made the remark at a news conference after a cabinet meeting approved the plan, known as the DPEF. He did not immediately elaborate.</p>
<p>Rome newsroom +396-6782505</p>
